# Domain modules

Code under `internal/<domain>/`. Wiring in [go-config-wiring.mdc](./go-config-wiring.mdc). Layout in [go-project-structure.mdc](./go-project-structure.mdc).

## Terms

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Domain | `internal/<domain>/` bounded context |
| Feature | Vertical slice; shares `models/`, `interfaces/` |
| Layer | `handler` → `service` → `repository` |

## Layout

```
internal/<domain>/
├── AGENTS.md
├── handler/<feature>_handler.go
├── interfaces/<feature>_interfaces.go
├── models/<feature>_models.go
├── repository/<feature>_repository.go
├── service/<feature>_service.go
├── service/<feature>_service_test.go
└── mocks/{interfaces,handler}/
```

Import: `<module>/internal/<domain>/handler`.

`AGENTS.md` documents the domain for agents; update on every change. See [go-module-ai-doc.mdc](./go-module-ai-doc.mdc). Service coverage **>80%**: [go-service-tests.mdc](./go-service-tests.mdc).

## Structs

Private implementation struct, exported `New*` returning an interface when the project uses interfaces.

```go
type orderService struct { repo interfaces.OrderRepository }

func NewOrderService(repo interfaces.OrderRepository) interfaces.OrderService {
    return &orderService{repo: repo}
}

func (s *orderService) GetByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*models.Order, error) {
    return s.repo.FindByID(ctx, id)
}
```

Routes and Dig registration belong in `config/`, not here.

## Layers

**interfaces/** — `Repository`, `Service`, and shared helpers (parser, validator). `context.Context` first on I/O. No HTTP imports. Handler interface either here or in `handler/`; one style per domain.

**models/** — DTOs, params, responses. Tags per project. No logic.

**repository/** — Persistence only. `New<Feature>Repository(...) <Feature>Repository`. Wrapped errors. No business rules.

**service/** — Business logic. Depends on interfaces only. `New<Feature>Service(...) interfaces.<Feature>Service`.

**handler/** — HTTP binding, validation, status codes. Calls service with `c.Request().Context()`. Map errors via `pkg/kit/wrapper` ([go-errors.mdc](./go-errors.mdc)). No SQL, no repository access. Shared parsers stay in `handler`.

## New feature

| File | Content |
|------|---------|
| `interfaces/<feature>_interfaces.go` | Repository, Service |
| `models/<feature>_models.go` | Types |
| `repository/`, `service/`, `handler/` | Implementations |
| `config/.../router/<feature>/` | `*<Feature>Router` |
| `config/.../injector/` | Provide chain |

One feature → one feature router in `config/`.

## Naming

| Item | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Packages | `handler`, `service`, `repository`, `interfaces`, `models` |
| Files | `<feature>_<layer>.go` |
| Types | `OrderService`, `orderService` |
| Constructors | `NewOrderService` |

## Interfaces

```go
type OrderRepository interface {
    FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*models.Order, error)
}

type OrderService interface {
    FindByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*models.Order, error)
}
```

Service may match Repository while delegating; diverge when rules accumulate.

## Workflow

1. Mirror an existing feature in the same repository
2. `models` → `interfaces` → `repository` → `service` → `handler`
3. mockery → service tests (coverage >80%)
4. Swagger on handlers; `swag init` if applicable
5. Register in injector; wire router
6. Update `AGENTS.md`
7. `go build ./...` and `go test ./internal/<domain>/...`

## Avoid

- Concrete cross-layer types instead of interfaces
- Logic, SQL, routes, or `Provide` in domain packages
- Import paths without `internal/`
- Package-level stateful functions
- Logger or HTTP setup in `internal/`
